@using ListingStudio.Web.Components.Articles

<p class="article-lede">
    Which kinds of home tour videos actually take off on TikTok? We looked at the real estate TikToks that news and trade
    outlets have reported with view and like counts, grouped them into campaign types, and compared them. The short
    version: surprise gets the most views, but a good home with a clear price gets the most likes.
</p>

<h2 id="answer">The short answer</h2>
<p>
    The biggest view counts belong to videos built on a surprise: a shocking home, a creator with a running bit, or an
    agent sprinting through the house. Those videos reach 8 million to 50 million views. A plain, good-looking walkthrough
    with a price hook, such as "What £750,000 buys in Leicestershire", gets fewer views (about 1.4 million to 7 million in
    the examples we found) but the highest like rate we could check: roughly 12% to 23% of viewers liked it, against about
    8% for the best-known shock video.
</p>
<p>
    Announcement posts, such as Just listed, Open house or Price drop, had no viral examples with published numbers at
    all. They are useful messages to add to a video, but they are not, on their own, a type of video people seek out.
</p>
<p class="article-note" data-testid="directional-note">
    Treat every number here as directional. No study compares home tour types on TikTok, so the figures come from
    individual videos reported in the press, each counted on the day it was written about. These are the videos that went
    viral; a typical real estate TikTok post earns about 3.1% total engagement per view
    (<a href="@Sources.DashSocial.Url" rel="noopener">Dash Social, H1 2025</a>).
</p>

